\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  Jesus' youthful day's events
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 we do not know much of it
\par the only one full of events
\par listen to carefully.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The story runs that Jesus
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 who did not know his father,
\par did not assume to be God's son
\par rather, humbled himself.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  When he became twelve years of age
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 He went to Jerusalem
\par He saw that his father was God
\par and people were in sin.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  He sensed that he was the saviour
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj and had the right to stay
\par in his father's  throne always
\par here on earth and in heaven.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  He helped too his father Joseph
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0\qj and became a skillful craftsman
\par respected him, his mother
\par and served and honoured them too
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.  He humbled himself for them all
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0\qj for pretty thirty years
\par stayed home and served them aright
\par loved and respected them in whole
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7.  Children, young men and women
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0\qj must also learn from Him
\par be humble as he, at home
\par towards your parents the same
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8.  It is only then that you all
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0\qj  shall grow in age and wisdom
\par  The favour the eternal God
\par \pard         and blessings from all people.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

